.IX Title "PMDANAMED 1"
.TH PMDANAMED 1 "Performance Co-Pilot" 7.2.0 "Performance Co-Pilot"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
pmdanamed \- BIND (named) PMDA
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBpmdanamed\fR is a Performance Metrics Domain Agent (PMDA) which
exports metric values from the BIND DNS server.
Further details on BIND can be found at http://isc.org/.
.SH INSTALLATION
.IX Header "INSTALLATION"
If you want access to the names and values for the named performance
metrics, do the following as root:
.PP
.Vb 2
\&        # cd $PCP_PMDAS_DIR/named
\&        # ./Install
.Ve
.PP
If you want to undo the installation, do the following as root:
.PP
.Vb 2
\&        # cd $PCP_PMDAS_DIR/named
\&        # ./Remove
.Ve
.PP
\&\fBpmdanamed\fR is launched by \fBpmcd\fR\|(1) and should never be executed
directly.  The Install and Remove scripts notify \fBpmcd\fR\|(1) when
the agent is installed or removed.
.SH "فایل‌ها (FILES)"
.IX Header "FILES"
.IP /var/named/data/named_stats.txt 4
.IX Item "/var/named/data/named_stats.txt"
statistics file showing values exported from named
.IP /var/named/chroot/var/named/data/named_stats.txt 4
.IX Item "/var/named/chroot/var/named/data/named_stats.txt"
chroot variant of statistics file showing values exported from named
.ie n .IP $PCP_PMDAS_DIR/named/Install 4
.el .IP \f(CR$PCP_PMDAS_DIR\fR/named/Install 4
.IX Item "$PCP_PMDAS_DIR/named/Install"
installation script for the \fBpmdanamed\fR agent
.ie n .IP $PCP_PMDAS_DIR/named/Remove 4
.el .IP \f(CR$PCP_PMDAS_DIR\fR/named/Remove 4
.IX Item "$PCP_PMDAS_DIR/named/Remove"
undo installation script for the \fBpmdanamed\fR agent
.ie n .IP $PCP_LOG_DIR/pmcd/named.log 4
.el .IP \f(CR$PCP_LOG_DIR\fR/pmcd/named.log 4
.IX Item "$PCP_LOG_DIR/pmcd/named.log"
default log file for error messages from \fBpmdanamed\fR
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBpmcd\fR\|(1), \fBnamed.conf\fR\|(5), \fBnamed\fR\|(8).
